      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:13oqevn'
    '|a||Three new cases to finish. A city caps taxi licences at 500, and a licence sells for a fortune. Which assumption of perfect competition fails?':
